# Native JSON source and textarea normalization

HTML textareas normalize CRLF and bare CR to LF. The native Flow view keeps the loaded or imported decoded source text separately from that normalized display. Validation, Save and Export use the backing text when the displayed text still matches it. This preserves an unchanged saved/imported source's line endings and whitespace. Once the displayed content differs, operations use that current edited display; node/wire edits deliberately reformat JSON. Other Unicode, including U+2028, astral characters and combining sequences, is not normalized by this comparison.

Deploy compares the displayed draft with the CR-only normalized **saved** text, then deploys the saved raw revision. A real content or whitespace change still requires Save first. An initial CRLF/bare-CR source therefore deploys without a false dirty warning. Unknown native metadata and the raw physical wires overwritten by virtual compilation remain retained.

Export captures the exact draft source and filename before validation. It refuses a late export if the view, input revision, displayed content or filename changed during that await. It does not export newer unvalidated input or an older backing document over a newer draft. Save commits its captured draft and advances the saved baseline, while retaining newer input across its response/list/preview awaits. Imported File.text() publication also refuses newer input or a closed view. Closing drops the raw backing reference and scrubs detached controls; it does not undo an already committed server operation.

The native controls remain disabled during an operation. Defensive tests that change a field while disabled are explicitly **programmatic DOM-model probes**, not evidence of real user typing into disabled controls. Blob contents are checked in model tests; actual browser download delivery is not claimed. File.text() decodes UTF-8, strips a UTF-8 BOM and replaces malformed bytes, so source-text preservation is not arbitrary original-file binary-byte preservation. Export encodes decoded text as UTF-8.

The raw backing, normalized textarea and temporary parsing/editing copies add allocations within the existing 4 MiB native-document bound. This is not a process-memory ceiling. Static graph/runtime/server budgets and semantics are unchanged from the frozen Link In/Link Out stage; no speed or memory superiority claim follows.

The preserved staged correction selector has **75 tests**: the previous 57 plus 14 unchanged negative/control bodies and four fresh adjacent publication boundaries. The initial native-normalizing model found 5 passes/9 failures on the original client. The exact bodies pass after the correction, including the actual root browser seed, CRLF, bare CR, LF, Unicode, real dirty differences, raw Export/Save/Import, held response and disposal controls. Original comparisons remain the three grouped checks containing 9 compiler fixtures, 7 handler cases and 8 full test-helper flows. The old 57-test receipt and the root's 7-pass/1-failed actual browser campaign remain immutable historical epochs. The independent model review passes 24 groups (14 retained bodies and 10 fresh controls). The separate normal-host browser review passes 12 observations, one file import and three exact 1,812-byte native downloads. Held-response, bare-CR browser and pending-disposal browser acceptance remain open. Installed-path test acceptance remains pending.


## Preserved source and finite evidence

The [static-link source provenance](results/native-link-textarea-followup/static-link-stage/frozen/source-provenance.json.snapshot), [publisher Apache-2.0 license](results/native-link-textarea-followup/static-link-stage/frozen/official-source/node-red-nodes/LICENSE.snapshot.snapshot), [runtime license](results/native-link-textarea-followup/static-link-stage/frozen/official-source/node-red-runtime/LICENSE.snapshot.snapshot) and [test-helper license](results/native-link-textarea-followup/static-link-stage/frozen/verification-source/node-red-node-test-helper/LICENSE.snapshot.snapshot) retain complete source notices. Compressed carriers and installed original dependencies remain local-only.

Historical native34/51-runtime/828-scalar, [author static57](results/native-link-textarea-followup/static-link-stage/frozen/validation.json.snapshot), [author corrected75](results/native-link-textarea-followup/textarea-correction/frozen/validation.json.snapshot), [independent model24](results/native-link-textarea-followup/independent-model-review/frozen/review-validation.json.snapshot), [negative browser8](results/native-link-textarea-followup/root-negative-browser/frozen/browser-observations.json.snapshot) and [corrected browser12](results/native-link-textarea-followup/root-corrected-browser/frozen/browser-observations.json.snapshot) stay separate source epochs. The author original groups contain9 compiler fixtures,7 handler cases and8 full test-helper flows per accepted campaign; the root static review separately records128 compiler calls. This publication planner runs none of those comparisons.

The corrected normal shared-host browser preserves exact raw CRLF across loaded Save and three actual downloads, one file import, static link connection/deployment isolation and reload persistence. The browser does not cover held transport responses, bare-CR input or pending disposal. Programmatic edits of disabled controls are defensive model probes, not real user typing evidence. No full Node-RED editor/runtime parity, security equivalence or superiority is established.
